# Each function runs once. A word of the instance lives as long as the program, and what closures have captured dies with them. So a text, an object, a list and a bigint stay where the collector can let them go:
# one field that holds a text keeps the whole scope, and a closure that holds a word (inner holds box) is kept like the word. Numbers, booleans and undefined are stored.
# RUN(COUNT): compile EnvironmentsPromotedToVariables mechanisms=all
# COUNT-NOT: statistic EnvironmentsPromotedToVariables 1
# RUN(TEXT): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# TEXT-NOT: EnterBodyThatRunsOnce
# RUN(OBJECT): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# OBJECT-NOT: PutModuleVariable
# RUN(LIST): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# LIST-NOT: PutModuleVariable
# RUN(BIGINT): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# BIGINT-NOT: PutModuleVariable
# RUN(HOLDER): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# HOLDER-NOT: PutModuleVariable
# RUN(NUMBERS): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# NUMBERS: EnterBodyThatRunsOnce
# NUMBERS: PutModuleVariable
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 2 n1! 2 2 5 6 14
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-PromotedEnvironments
# HELD: 2 n1! 2 2 5 6 14
